          Here:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the top functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocontinuous+functor"} colimit-preserving functor
                that makes the top
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} triangle commute
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PresheafAsColimitOfRepresentables"} (2)
                that every presheaf is a colimit of representables.
            %li
              %p
                the bottom functor is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
                of the slice category, which means
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HomInSliceCategoryAsFiberProduct"} (3)
