            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p Observe that:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Since representables are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+objects"} cofibrant
                  (evidently so in the projective model structure, since
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+Kan+fibrations"} acyclic Kan fibrations
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a{:href => "acyclic+Kan+fibration#AcyclicKanFibrationsAreSurjective"} are surjective
                  %a{:href => "enriched+model+category#PullbackPowerAxiom"} pullback-power axiom
                  in the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi sSet
                            %mi Qu
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Qu}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi sSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSh(\mathcal{C})
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  = succeed "-functor" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                  is a right Quillen functor on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+model+categories"} slice model categories
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi sSet
                          %mi Qu
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Qu}
                  (by
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "slice+model+structure#LeftBaseChangeQuillenAdjunction"} this Prop.
            %p
              Together this implies that their composite
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SliceHomOfPresheavesAsFiberOfPlainHom"} (5)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ken+Brown%27s+lemma"} Ken Brown's lemma
              (
              %a{:href => "factorization+lemma#KenBrownLemma"}> here
              ) it follows that the right adjoint preserves weak equivalences between
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
              %em reflects
              weak equivalences between fibrant objects, in that a morphism between fibrant objects on the left is a weak equivalence if and only if its image under the right adjoint functor is a weak equivalences. Since the functor is also an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheAdjointEquivalenceInOrdinaryCategoryTheory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction"} derived adjunction
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy categories
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            %p
              To see this remaining claim (that the right adjoint reflects weak equivalences between fibrant objects) consider a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi sPsh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi y
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \,\in\, sPsh(\mathcal{C})_{/y_{\mathcal{C}}(X)}
              between fibrations such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \xrightarrow{\phi} X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/X}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SliceHomOfPresheavesAsFiberOfPlainHom"} (5)
              of its values on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \,\in\, \mathcal{C}
              is a weak equivalence:
            %svg{:height => "74.438", :viewbox => "0 0 374.662 74.438", :width => "374.662", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
