            %p
              Here the right vertical morphisms are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
              by the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sPSh(\mathcal{C})\big( y_{\mathcal{C}}(U),\, - \big)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
              as in the first item above. Therefore – since this holds for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              %a{:href => "slice+model+structure#SimplicialWeakEquivalencesInSliceDetectedFiberwise"} this Prop.
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f(U)
                    \\,\simeq\,
                    \\mathrm{PSh}(\mathcal{C})
                    \\big(
                    y_{\mathcal{C}}(U)
                    ,\,
                    f
                    \\big)
              is a weak equivalence. And since this holds for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \,\in\, \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a weak equivalence in the slice of the projective model structure.
          %h5#locally Locally
          %p
            We now promote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            in the previous section to the case of Čech-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structures+on+simplicial+presheaves"}> local model structures on simplicial presheaves
            \.
          %p
            Recall that these are obtained as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localization"} left Bousfield localization
            of the (say)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure"} projective model structure
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            with respect to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerves"} Čech nerves
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+families"} covering families
          %p We reuse the notation of the previous section.
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              of
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialLocalSectionsIsRightQuillen"}
              descends to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              of the corresponding Čech-local projective model structures.
