          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Both
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper"} left proper
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial"} combinatorial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localizations"} left Bousfield localizations
              with respect to arbitrary sets of morphisms.
            %p
              We localize both sides with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerves"} Čech nerves
              of respective covering families. Observe that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerves"} Čech nerves
              of covering families in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/X}
              are mapped to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerves"} Čech nerves
              of covering families in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sPSh(\mathcal{C})
              and therefore also in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sPSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi y
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sPSh(\mathcal{C})_{y_{\mathcal{C}}(X)}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              between localized
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            %p
              It remains to show that this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            %p
              It suffices to show that the right adjoint reflects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
              between
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
              are objectwise
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
              that satisfy the appropriate variant of the
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  homotopy descent property
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/homotopy+descent+property"} ?
          %p
            %br/
          %h4#SimplicialpresheavesSlicedOverOneTruncatedObjects Over 1-truncated objects
          %p
            Over a 1-truncated object (hence over a simplicial presheaf with values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+nerve"} simplicial nerve
            of a
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the slice category needs to be generalized to the homotopy slice, now given by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
                (in groupoids);
            %li
              %p
                the right adjoint needs to be generalized from forming
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SliceHomOfPresheavesAsFiberOfPlainHom"} (5)
                to forming
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
          %p
            This happens in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Hollander08"} Hollander 2008, Def. 5.1
          %p
            The resulting Quillen equivalences for the global
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Hollander08"} Hollander 2008, Them. 5.2
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Hollander08"} Hollander 2008, Thm. 6.2
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#InInfinityCategoryTheory
            In
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            All the natural equivalences used in a category-theoretic proof such as of Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StatementInPlainCategoryTheoryOverAnyPresheaf"}
            above also hold in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-category theory
          %p
            More explicitly, since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} identifies
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}>
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-category
            ) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+categories"} combinatorial model categories
            (such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories+of+simplicial+presheaves"} model categories of simplicial presheaves
            and their
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+model+structures"} slice model structures
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"}
                presentable
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialLocalSectionsIsRightQuillen"}
            immediately
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} implies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+Quillen+adjunction"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} present
            the equivalence of
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p Either way, we obtain the following conclusion (and again this hold verbatim also over non-representable base presheaves):
          %p
          #EquivalenceOfInfinityCategories.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (fundamental theorem of
                = succeed "-presheaf" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
                small
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
